The core idea

The solution is not:

"10 jobs are unpaused."

It is:

"Every environment has a default state, and any job can be an exception."

That means your configuration remains flexible whether you have:

40 jobs → 10 running
40 jobs → 20 running
40 jobs → 2 running
1,000 jobs → 100 running
1,000 jobs → 50 running

You simply change variables.yml; schedules.py doesn't need to change.

One implementation point I would keep strict: the exact syntax/API for reading a complex DAB variable in your existing schedules.py needs to match the Databricks Bundles/Python version in your repository. The architecture and precedence above are the design; that API detail should be taken from your existing working mutator rather than guessed.
